{"id": "EUVD-2026-101713", "enisaUuid": "303cfd60-b601-37d4-b778-4ba44c3f51c2", "description": "FreeRDP before 3.32.0 fails to close prior serial handles in serial_process_irp_create, allowing a malicious RDP server to exhaust file descriptors. Attackers can send repeated serial IRP_MJ_CREATE requests to accumulate descriptors and terminate the client at the CommReadFile FD_SETSIZE assertion.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T22:52:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:12:12", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-mqxv-c882-m8w9", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-before-3.32.0-denial-of-service-via-serial-irp-mj-create"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5v64-xvh3-p6jj", "CVE-2026-110830"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8febc272-1c83-3ef2-8318-eb31d1646ce9", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "2.0.0-rc0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "18a0996f-77a7-3f38-9a40-2293c58dab20", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}